  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "14. Objectives",
    "ruleNumber": "14.01",
    "summary": "A mission using objectives gives their locations on the deployment map. Measure to or from an **objective**'s nearest point. An objective is either:\n\n- a **terrain objective**: the **[terrain area itself](vsdata:core-rule/placing-terrain)** at that location\n- where no terrain area is there, a 40mm objective marker centred on the location\n\nModels may pass through a marker or end a move on it. A model is in range of a marker within 3 inches horizontally and 5 inches vertically of its nearest point.\n\nSee **[Level of Control](vsdata:core-rule/level-of-control)** for who holds an objective.",
